# Sustainable Fashion Research Plan Revision Update Improvements<br>
<br>
## Introduction<br>
This research plan aims to explore innovative ways to source sustainable materials for the fashion industry. We will discuss potential suppliers, assess their environmental impact, and identify opportunities for improvement.<br>
<br>
## Objectives<br>
1. Identify 5 potential suppliers of sustainable materials.<br>
2. Evaluate the environmental impact of each supplier using a scoring system (e.g., carbon footprint, water usage).<br>
3. Research innovative technologies for material conversion (e.g., upcycling, recycling).<br>
<br>
## Methodology<br>
<br>
### Step 1: Supplier Identification<br>
We will research and identify 5 potential suppliers of sustainable materials through online directories and industry reports.<br>
<br>
### Step 2: Environmental Impact Assessment<br>
Using a scoring system, we will evaluate the environmental impact of each supplier based on their carbon footprint, water usage, and other relevant factors.<br>
<br>
### Step 3: Innovative Technologies Research<br>
We will research innovative technologies for material conversion, including upcycling and recycling methods.<br>
<br>
## Expected Outcomes<br>
<br>
* A list of 5 potential suppliers of sustainable materials.<br>
* An assessment of the environmental impact of each supplier using a scoring system.<br>
* Identification of opportunities for improvement in sourcing sustainable materials.<br>
```<br>
